Z||000000||Mr.Frosty||04-05-2001||03:27 PM||||Is there an alternative for the T-handle automatic shift knob in the fiero?I was looking for something that looked like a fakey Manual shift knob.I'm sure I'm not the only one here that's interested.I created an elaborate one awhile back out of wood that was small,contoured,and had a push button.It had a nice finish,and was stained and varnished,but I am going to make a better one soon.It takes way to long to make them though.I saw someone with a ferrari rebody that had one made out of aluminum and it looked trick.Just throwin it out there.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top <BR>85 GT Turbo||||reg||5
Z||000001||danny boy||04-05-2001||04:04 PM|||| the knob from the CAmaro/Firebirds will work. I'm sure other GM products will, too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||04-05-2001||04:05 PM||||JC Whitney sells aftermarket auto knobs made of aluminum.. also, camaro or cavalier knobs can be used as well. They have the button on top, and look more like a manual knob than the T auto one.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
